6921.7 gpu: world feature feature=bumpmap declared=54 visible=54 resolved=54 missing=0 first=HIMALAYAN/HIMALAYA_ROCK01_BLEND04 resource=materials/himalayan/himalaya_rock01_ssbump.vtf reason=the materials name 25 distinct $bumpmap textures, so the one sampler slot the pass started with cannot apply each material's own; per-material binding is the --world-material-bump switch, and with it on the 29 that do not set $ssbump sample their own tile through a texinfo-axis tangent basis while the 25 that do stay refused (see the $ssbump row)
6921.7 gpu: world feature feature=bumpmap2 declared=5 visible=5 resolved=5 missing=0 first=HIMALAYAN/HIMALAYA_ROCK01_BLEND04 resource=materials/Nature/snow_full001_normal.vtf reason=$bumpmap2 is layer 2's normal map: it is lerped into layer 1's normal by the vertex blend weight, so it is sampled only when --world-material-bump and --world-bump2 are both on; with either off it is refused, not silently replaced by layer 1's; 1/5 of those materials also declare $ssbump, so their second-layer texel is a bumpBasis weight and stays refused even with both switches on (--world-bump2-texture measures the layer with a diagnostic normal map instead)
6921.7 gpu: world feature feature=ssbump declared=25 visible=25 resolved=25 missing=0 first=HIMALAYAN/HIMALAYA_ROCK01_BLEND04 resource=himalayan/himalaya_rock01_ssbump reason=$ssbump selects `BUMPMAP == 2`, where the texel is not a signed normal but three bumpBasis weights against three lightmap directions; this pass samples one lightmap and one tangent-space normal, so these materials are refused by name even when --world-material-bump is on
6921.7 gpu: world feature feature=detail declared=28 visible=28 resolved=0 missing=28 first=FRANKENIZER/CRYPTWALL2A resource=materials/overlays/detail001.vmt reason=detail layers are the --world-detail switch: the detail material's $basetexture is sampled at the atlas uv scaled by $detailscale and combined with the albedo by $detailblendmode; with the switch off the layer is refused
